You are describing a solution in search of a problem here.

Just leave the artifacts off-branch (Mines or Soko), or throw them in
the water at the Castle, or put in a chest (doesn't have to be locked,
monsters don't loot containers), or... the possibilities are actually
relatively endless.  There's no need to add something whose sole purpose
would be to solve a solved problem.

> As you discussed with Jym, it could be like destroy armor in
> doing damage proofing.  Certain artifacts don't come fixed - Sting
> and Orcrist (and ones found on the floor usually in shops?)

Sting and Orcrist are junk and I am sad to see them in my games;
being able to fireproof them will not make them any more pleasant to 
pick up out of someone's bones file.  (plus, they're wood, so already
resistant to rust monsters and rust traps.)

Artifacts on the floor in shops are worth using confused enchant weapon
for, since I usually have plenty of spares of those that I just turn
into blank scrolls normally.  Until then, I just don't hit rust monsters 
with the weapon -- since rust monsters do no physical damage, beating
them to death with your fists (or just going around them) is trivial.

